([STRONG]Chapter 3: Norms for Land and Spatial Infrastructure) Tj
0 -16 Td
([STRONG]Section 3.1: Minimum Land Requirements for Technical Institutions) Tj
0 -16 Td
(For Engineering and Technology institutions, the minimum contiguous land requirement is 2.5 acres) Tj
0 -16 Td
(in designated Urban areas \(Mega/Metro cities\) and 4.0 acres in Rural areas. The land must be free from) Tj
0 -16 Td
(any encumbrances and owned or leased on long-term basis for a minimum duration of thirty years.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
([STRONG]Section 3.2: Carpet Area and Built-up Space Norms) Tj
0 -16 Td
(The prescribed total built-up carpet area for technical institutions depends on applied student intake.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(For applied intake exceeding 120 students, the minimum required built-up area is 4,000 square metres.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Institutions with intake of 120 or fewer students must possess at least 2,500 square metres of area.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
([STRONG]Section 3.3: Laboratory and Workshop Requirements) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Institutions must provide minimum one specialised laboratory or practical workshop per thirty technical) Tj
0 -16 Td
(intake. Every technical institution must possess a baseline minimum of four fully equipped laboratories.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Blueprints exhibiting a shortfall of more than 50% laboratories trigger an on-site scrutiny inspection.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
([STRONG]Section 3.4: Computer Centre and Digital Library Norms) Tj
0 -16 Td
(A dedicated Computer Centre with a terminal-to-student ratio of 1:4 for technical courses is mandatory.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(High-speed broadband internet connectivity and subscription to national e-journal consortia are required.) Tj
0 -16 Td
() Tj
0 -16 Td
([STRONG]Section 3.5: Barrier-free Environment and Accessibility) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Institutions must provide barrier-free infrastructure including ramps, lifts, and dedicated accessible) Tj
0 -16 Td
(washrooms for differently-abled persons in accordance with the Persons with Disabilities Act.) Tj
0 -16 Td
